values ('a2b3c4d5-7e8f-4a52-9b12-2c3d4e5f6a22', 'aging-gerontological-social-work', 'Aging / Gerontological Social Work', 'Aging / Gerontological Social Work prepares students to practice with older adults, caregivers, families, organizations, and communities in a rapidly aging society. Students learn aging demographics, life-course development, physical and cognitive aging, psychosocial aging, caregiving, long-term services, elder mistreatment, end-of-life care, aging policy, diversity, and evidence-informed social work practice. The course emphasizes person-in-environment assessment, dignity, autonomy, cultural humility, anti-oppressive practice, interprofessional care, and practical navigation of aging-service systems.');

